WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
In the Ming dynasty there was a medical scholar named Li Shizhen, who from his youth resolved to organize all knowledge of medicines.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.600
The shelves were filled with medical books, and the table held all kinds of dried medicinal herbs.

3
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.880
To learn about real medicinal herbs, he traveled through high mountains and fields, collecting and studying medicines himself.

4
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.080
Carrying a bamboo basket on his back, he climbed a steep mountain slope, and his sweat soaked through his clothes.

5
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:28.120
He carefully observed every kind of medicinal herb, and earnestly recorded their appearance, properties, and uses.

6
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.480
He held an herb up to his nose to smell it, and then drew its appearance in his notebook.

7
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.520
After many years of effort, he finally completed the great medical book, the Compendium of Materia Medica.

8
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:44.040
The book recorded a large number of medicines and helped countless doctors and patients; its contents were extremely rich.

9
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.360
Young doctors studied it earnestly, hoping to cure even more patients.

10
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:57.280
Li Shizhen became a celebrity known in every household, and his great book has been passed down to this day.
